# Template: the release workflow fills in @VERSION@.
Name:           plasma-network-health
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Network health indicator for KDE Plasma

License:        MIT
URL:            https://github.com/AtmanActive/plasma-network-health
Source0:        %{name}-%{version}-source.tar.gz

BuildRequires:  gcc-c++
BuildRequires:  cmake >= 3.16
BuildRequires:  systemd-rpm-macros

Recommends:     plasma-workspace

%description
A Plasma 6 widget that answers one question at a glance: is my network still
fine? Each destination you configure gets a round indicator next to its name,
green while it answers pings quickly enough and red when it stops. In the
system tray it collapses to a single target icon coloured by overall health.

All probing happens in a separate backend process, which multiplexes every
destination onto one ICMP socket per address family and sends every probe that
is due in a single wakeup. Nothing the network does can stall plasmashell,
because the widget itself never performs a network operation: it only re-reads
a small state file the backend publishes.

%prep
%autosetup -n %{name}-%{version}

%build
%cmake
%cmake_build

%install
%cmake_install

%files
%license LICENSE
%doc README.md
%{_bindir}/plasma-network-healthd
%{_datadir}/plasma/plasmoids/com.github.atmanactive.networkhealth/
%{_userunitdir}/plasma-network-healthd.service

